{
  "rationale": "Use a simple capability plant that admits all given sensor and motion events, then encode the exploration policy in a small deterministic specification. The specification gives exactly one controllable action in each non-terminal decision/recovery state, keeps all uncontrollable events total, uses random_walk in clear exploration, routes every obstacle through a turn-recovery state, prefers directed short turns over scans, and returns quickly to exploration when path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model sensing and actuation permissively in the plant so the supervisor policy is expressed cleanly in the specification.",
    "Use one-shot commit states for random_walk, move_forward, and directed turns; self-loop path_clear in commit states and let obstacle events preempt only when safety-critical.",
    "Bias toward coverage by alternating clear exploration random_walk with short forward progress, while obstacle_left prefers clockwise recovery and obstacle_right prefers counterclockwise recovery.",
    "Reserve full_rotate only for a dedicated blocked-front escape state and do not use it in clear/search/path_clear-reached states."
  ],
